## Changes since previous release

### Added

- Added hardware acceleration for _chacha20_ and _poly1305_ algorithms (adopted from [libsodium](https://github.com/jedisct1/libsodium)
- Added new pragmas `mc_cpu_info`, `mc_aes_info`, and `mc_chacha20_hwaccel`
- Added readline/editline support for SQLite3MC shell on Linux platforms
- Added tests for the cryptographic primitives (contributed by @mtrossbach)
- Added encryption of temporary files with a random key per file (@utelle and @mtrossbach)
- Added pragma `encrypt_temp_db` for forcing encryption of temporary database files

### Changed

- Based on SQLite version 3.54.0
- Reordered MAC verification and decryption process (decrypt only after successful verification of MAC)
- Removed unconditional define for symbol `SQLITE3MC_ENABLE_VLE`
- Modernized `sqlite3mcSecureZeroMemory()` (contributed by @matbech)
- Improved random number generator
- Removed dead code (issue #256)  
  The use case that HMACs are not generated and stored in the database for cipher schemes which include a HMAC is not supported any longer. Actually, this feature was not operational since SQLite3MC was separated from wxSQLite3.
- Compare SQLCipher HMAC values in constant time (contributed by @mtrossbach)
- Adjusted target attribute for GCC for AES on aarch64  
  The target attribute _"+crypto"_ was not set even if `aarch64` hardware was detected. That is, AES hardware support was not used on `aarch64` platforms (see PR #262).
- Hardened the Linux entropy source (contributed by @mtrossbach)
- Use fast key erasure in the ChaCha20 random number generator (contributed by @mtrossbach)
- Keep temporary data in memory unless `SQLITE_TEMP_STORE` is explicitly set

### Fixed

- Fixed issue #263 - The not existing function `explicit_bzero()` was referenced for Android API 28+. Use function `memset_explicit()` for Android API 34+.
- Fixed issue #265 - Fix WASM entropy source when HEAPU8 is not exported (contributed by @mtrossbach)
- Fixed issue #272 - Do not drop read errors of the real file (contributed by @mtrossbach)
- Fixed issue #280 - Improved check for compatibility with SQLite's backup feature
- Fixed issue #282 - Improved handling of legacy cipher modes
- Fixed issue #283 - Salt in raw key now takes precedence over salt in the database header.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> :pushpin: The _amalgamation source package_ including `configure` is _still_ **experimental**. :pushpin:
> Currently, only POSIX compliant systems are supported. Support files for building on Windows are included, but will only be adapted if the need arises.
Please report any issue you may experience using the [GitHub issue tracker](https://github.com/utelle/SQLite3MultipleCiphers/issues).
❗ Please share your experiences with this source package. TIA. ❗ 

**Notes**
This release contains the following precompiled binaries:
- SQLite3 binaries for Windows (SQLite3 shell and DLLs) _with_ resp. _without_ enabled ICU support in variants for 32-bit and 64-bit Windows. The SQLite3 shell applications support the [SQLite Archive](https://www.sqlite.org/sqlar.html) feature,
- Source code amalgamation (_amalgamation_) - a single C source file and a single C header file,
- Source code amalgamation (_autoconf_) - a single C source file and a single C header file - including a `configure` script for POSIX compliant systems,
- Precompiled SQLite Android library (see [SQLite Android Bindings](https://www.sqlite.org/android/doc/trunk/www/index.wiki)),
- Precompiled bundle of `sqlite3.wasm` and its JavaScript APIs, ready for use in web applications (see [SQLite3 WebAssembly](https://sqlite.org/wasm/)).

## Verification

Release artifacts were built by GitHub Actions and are published with GitHub Artifact Attestations for provenance verification.

The `SHA256SUMS` file containing the checksums of the release artifacts is additionally signed using [Sigstore Cosign](https://docs.sigstore.dev/cosign/).

To verify the integrity and authenticity of the checksum file, install Cosign and run:

```sh
cosign verify-blob \
  --certificate sqlite3mc-{SQLITE3MC_VERSION}-SHA256SUMS.pem \
  --signature sqlite3mc-{SQLITE3MC_VERSION}-SHA256SUMS.sig \
  --certificate-identity-regexp '^https://github.com/utelle/SQLite3MultipleCiphers/.*' \
  --certificate-oidc-issuer https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com \
  sqlite3mc-{SQLITE3MC_VERSION}-SHA256SUMS
```
